## Overview

PHMGen™ is a console application for procedural generation of realistic heightmaps. The program employs a comprehensive approach, simulating geological processes such as plate tectonics, erosion, sedimentation, and other phenomena to produce plausible terrain.

Heightmaps generated by the program are suitable for use in game engines (Unreal Engine, Unity), 3D editors, and landscape visualization systems.

The program supports generating both local terrain maps and entire planetary worlds—featuring a tectonic plate and continent simulation system.

### Key Features

- Multi-stage generation with the ability to enable/disable each stage  
- Plate tectonics simulation with convergent, divergent, and transform boundaries  
- Thermal and hydraulic erosion for realistic rivers and slopes  
- Batch generation of multiple maps in a single run  
- Export to 8-bit and 16-bit PNG  
- Multithreading for accelerated computation  
- Flexible configuration via a configuration file  
- Localization (Russian/English)  
- Reproducibility through a seed value  

### System Requirements

| Component | Requirement |
|-----------|-------------|
| OS        | Windows 10+ (earlier versions not tested) |
| RAM       | From ~7 MB in idle to 1.8 GB under default settings (8K resolution) |

### Quick Start

1. Run `PHMGen.exe`  
2. On first launch, choose the configuration file language (1 — Russian, 2 — English)  
3. Select map resolution (1–5, from 512 to 8192)  
4. Specify whether to use odd resolution (Y/N)  
5. Choose export format (1 — 8-bit, 2 — 16-bit PNG)  
6. Enter the number of maps to generate  
7. Wait for the process to complete  
8. The generated heightmap will be placed in the program folder  

### Generation Stages

The program executes generation in the following order:

| # | Stage                     | Description                         |
|---|---------------------------|-------------------------------------|
| 1 | Tectonics Simulation      | Plate creation and boundary modeling |
| 2 | Base Terrain              | Fractal noise (ridged FBM)          |
| 3 | Continents                | Separation of land and ocean        |
| 4 | Additional Features        | Volcanoes, craters, plateaus        |
| 5 | Domain Warping            | Organic shapes                      |
| 6 | Thermal Erosion           | Slope smoothing                     |
| 7 | Hydraulic Erosion         | Rivers, streams, and valleys        |
| 8 | Sedimentation             | Accumulation of deposits in lows    |
| 9 | Altitude Detail           | Height-based detail enhancement     |

Each stage can be enabled or disabled through the configuration file.

## Configuration

The configuration file is created automatically on first launch and contains parameters for all generation stages.

### Seed

The seed (`seed`) serves as the primary identifier for generation. Using the same seed with identical parameters produces reproducible results.

#### Special Notes on Seed Usage

- **Random seed generation**: set `seed = -1`  
- **Similarity in batch generation**: when generating multiple maps in one run, seeds will be similar, producing visually comparable maps.

